/**
 * @mainpage Developer Guide 
 * 
 * @section dev_guide_summary Summary
 *
 * This developer guide is intended for users who seek to implement the Lime Suite NG library into custom applications, or who want to contribute to the development and
 * distribution of Lime Suite NG and its software components.
 *
 * Developers who seek to implement Lime Suite NG into custom applications are recommended to review the ``Introduction`` and ``Library`` pages.
 * The ``Introduction`` page provides flowcharts and class diagrams that provide information about the communication control flow and class relationships of the Lime Suite NG library.
 * The ``Library`` page provides a reference to the Lime Suite NG library API, a development guide for beginning and experienced developers, as well as other important development
 * information and notes.
 *
 * Developers who seek to contribute to the development and distribution of Lime Suite NG are recommended to review the ``Tools`` and ``Distribution`` pages. The ``Tools`` page
 * provides information about various development tools that can be used to increase the efficiency of the Lime Suite NG development process. The ``Distribution`` page provides information
 * about packaging and distribution of Lime Suite NG and its software components.
 * 
 * ``GUI tool`` page is intended for engineers who seek to use a Lime Suite NG provided software tool for advanced LimeSDR device configurations.
 * 
 * The ``LMS API (Legacy)`` page provides limited documentation support for legacy software. It is recommended to use the new Lime Suite NG library and its API. Some LMS API to 
 * Lime Suite NG API porting guidelines are provided in the ``Library`` page.
 * 
 * Topics of interest:
 * <ol>
 *     <li> @ref diagrams_intro </li>
 *     <li> @ref limesuiteng_api_ref_top "Library" </li>
 *     <li> @ref dev_tools_index "Tools" </li>
 *     <li> @ref software_distribution </li>
 *     <li> @ref gui_tool_index </li>
 *     <li> @ref lms_api_index </li>
 * </ol>
 * 
 */